Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES  
  – "feature_type": filter to only the administrative boundaries drawn as multipolygons.  
  – "all_tags"     : JSON array to locate tags where key = 'boundary' and value = 'administrative'.  
  – "geometry"     : WKB geometry ‒ convert with TO_GEOGRAPHY() to test spatial relations.  
  – "osm_id" / "osm_way_id": returned OpenStreetMap identifier of each boundary.  

• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_NODES  
  – "all_tags"     : JSON array to locate tags where key = 'amenity'.  
  – "latitude","longitude": build GEOGRAPHY points with ST_MAKEPOINT() if "geometry" is NULL.  
  – "geometry"     : WKB point ‒ preferred when present.  
  – "id"           : node id, used only for reference / counting.  

Typical conditions  
1. "feature_type" = 'multipolygons'  
2. "boundary"‑tag exists with value 'administrative'  
3. in nodes: an entry with key = 'amenity' (value can be anything)  
4. Spatial test: ST_CONTAINS( TO_GEOGRAPHY(boundary.geometry) , node_point ) = TRUE  

Below are 10 exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (all capped with LIMIT 20) that step from inspection to the final answer search.

